; The four load-time rejections. `member-name` widens the declaration slot
; to "symbol or number", which is all a type can say; *which* numbers are
; spellings is a semantic question, so the loader owns it — the same split
; `(fixed N)` uses.
;
;   * `bad-unitless` — a number with no unit. A bare magnitude is not a
;     name, and accepting one would make `(member-set :values [1 2 3])`
;     look like an enum of integers.
;   * `bad-magnitude` — negative. Fractional and above-2^53 magnitudes are
;     rejected the same way: the cap is the range where the canonical
;     spelling has one text form in every host, which matters because the
;     name reaches the exported JSON-Schema enum and the `.d.ts` union.
;   * `bad-underlying` — on a `:string` underlying the members are string
;     literals, so no numeric value can ever reach them. Dead declaration,
;     said out loud rather than left looking effective.
;   * `bad-duplicate` — `2d` and `02d` canonicalise to the same name *and*
;     the same identity. The check is on the pair, since that is what the
;     validator matches on.
;   * `bad-duplicate-compact` — the same collision in the *other* authoring
;     shape. Both spellings of a member set run the same scan; the compact
;     one is the shape most schemas use, and it is where canonicalisation
;     makes a duplicate hardest to see by eye.
;
; A bare literal stands in for a document body: the plugin failed to load,
; so the host drops it entirely, and any `(texture …)` here would add an
; `unknown_form` cascade that says nothing about the declarations.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.3"
  (value-kind :name bad-unitless :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [1 2 3]))

  (value-kind :name bad-magnitude :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set (member :name -1d)))

  (value-kind :name bad-underlying :underlying string
    :members (member-set (member :name 2d)))

  (value-kind :name bad-duplicate :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set
      (member :name 2d)
      (member :name 02d)))

  (value-kind :name bad-duplicate-compact :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [2d 2.0d])))

42
